<holoml version="0.3">
  <head>
    <title>About the ocean tunnel</title>
    <meta name="description" content="What this aquarium is, what it shows of HoloML 0.3, what it is made of, and where to find HoloML." />
    <meta name="author" content="The HoloML Authors" />
  </head>
  <scene background="#0e2633">
    <viewpoint position="0 1.4 1.9" look-at="0 1.3 -0.7" />
    <light type="ambient" intensity="0.7" color="#cfe6ee" />
    <light type="directional" position="2 6 4" look-at="0 0 0" intensity="1.2" color="#eef8ff" />
    <model src="models/gallery.glb" position="0 0 -15.2" />
    <model src="models/wall.glb" position="0 0 4.95" scale="10.6 3.4 0.3" />
    <model src="models/wall.glb" position="-5.15 0 1.8" scale="0.3 3.4 6.3" />
    <model src="models/wall.glb" position="5.15 0 1.8" scale="0.3 3.4 6.3" />
    <model src="models/wall.glb" position="-3.85 0 -1.35" scale="2.3 3.4 0.3" />
    <model src="models/wall.glb" position="3.85 0 -1.35" scale="2.3 3.4 0.3" />
    <model src="models/shell.glb" position="-1.9 0.9 -0.6" rotation="0 30 0" scale="2.5" />

    <label position="0 2.3 -0.7" size="0.16" color="#8fd3ee">Ocean tunnel</label>

    <panel position="-0.62 1.6 -0.7" width="1.1" size="0.04" color="#1f2328" background="#f4f7f8">
      About this aquarium

      The ocean tunnel is an example of HoloML 0.3, an open markup language for 3D pages. The tank, the tunnel, the gallery, the rocks, the plants, and this page are written in HoloML: the water that everything is seen through, the light that plays over the sand, the bubbles heard from where they rise, the places to go to, and the Feed button. One script swims the fish, lets the bubbles rise, and drops the food.

      The fish are real kinds, and what the board says of them is true; the aquarium is made up.
    </panel>
    <panel position="0.62 1.6 -0.7" width="1.1" size="0.031" color="#1f2328" background="#f4f7f8">
      Made with

      The fish, under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/) unless said: the great white shark and the grey snapper from the Babylon.js asset library, by the Babylon.js authors; from Sketchfab, as Objaverse copied them: the hawksbill sea turtle by Bindestrek, the gilt-head bream by BlueMesh, the Atlantic mackerel by Amy Scott-Murray, the tuna by GoldenZtuff, the clownfish by zixisun02, and the copperband butterflyfish by Dsanchez13; and the barramundi by Microsoft, from the Khronos glTF Sample Assets (CC0). Each is sized, and those that did not swim were given a swim.

      The boulders, the log, the shell, and the sand are from Poly Haven (CC0). The tank, the tunnel, the plants, the bubbles, the food, and the sounds are made by the site's own script, tools/prepare.mjs. models/CREDITS.md has every name and address.
    </panel>

    <a href="https://github.com/srajpal/holoml/blob/main/SPEC.md">
      <panel position="-0.9 0.78 -0.7" width="0.8" size="0.05" color="#ffffff" background="#1d6fa5">The HoloML specification</panel>
    </a>
    <a href="https://github.com/srajpal/holoml/tree/main/examples/aquarium">
      <panel position="0 0.78 -0.7" width="0.8" size="0.05" color="#ffffff" background="#1d6fa5">This aquarium's source</panel>
    </a>
    <a href="https://github.com/srajpal/holoml/blob/main/examples/aquarium/models/CREDITS.md">
      <panel position="0.9 0.78 -0.7" width="0.8" size="0.05" color="#ffffff" background="#1d6fa5">Every credit</panel>
    </a>
    <a href="index.holoml">
      <panel position="0 0.5 -0.7" width="0.8" size="0.05" color="#ffffff" background="#5b6472">Back to the tunnel</panel>
    </a>
  </scene>
</holoml>
